      "lineNbr": 96,
      "author": {
        "id": 5065
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-08-17T22:54:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m fine with that too, even though our Cache interface as-is isn\u0027t suitable for pre-populating anything, since it\u0027s so opaque.\n\nBut for performance, no need to check the policy func for a cert we have cached.\n\nAlso, start by documenting what it does (\"controls access\"), not immediately jumping to how it does so (\"is evaluated\").\n\n  // HostPolicy controls which domains the Manager will attempt\n  // to retrieve new certs for. It does not affect cached certs.\n  // If nil, ....\n  // If non-nil, HostPolicy is called before retrieving a new cert.\n  // If it returns an error, XXXX.",
      "parentUuid": "bb944b51_d35c8389",
